212
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:38,268
isEmail, on the other hand, is easy to read

213
00:08:38,268 --> 00:08:40,595
and there is no room for interpretation. If

214
00:08:40,595 --> 00:08:43,644
I call a function called isEmail, it's clear

215
00:08:43,644 --> 00:08:45,474
that I wanna find out if something is an

216
00:08:45,506 --> 00:08:48,379
email or not. I wanna get back true or false

217
00:08:48,379 --> 00:08:48,571
here.

218
00:08:49,342 --> 00:08:51,958
Now for includes@, it's technically clear

219
00:08:52,086 --> 00:08:54,301
